{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.IdentityIHLFBridge","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall.three_blockEntry_independent_p21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall.three_blockEntry_independent_p21","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/SeminormalDimSmall.lean#L161-L189","doc":"**Three block-reading functionals at (2,1) are linearly independent** — the\nexact complement of `three_supported_traceFunctionals_dependent`, which says any\nthree *trace-factoring* ones there are dependent. Witnessed by matrix units:\neach functional is 1 on its own and 0 on the others. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall.blockEntry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall.blockEntry","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/SeminormalDimSmall.lean#L155-L159","doc":"Read entry `(i,j)` of the block at `lam`. Unlike `traceFunctional`, this sees\nthe block itself rather than only its trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall.indistinguishable_p21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall.indistinguishable_p21","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/SeminormalDimSmall.lean#L122-L130","doc":"And every trace-factoring functional at `(2,1)` — the Markov trace included —\nis blind to that difference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall.trace_does_not_separate_p21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall.trace_does_not_separate_p21","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/SeminormalDimSmall.lean#L116-L120","doc":"At `(2,1)` the block traces do not separate decompositions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall.not_two_le_seminormalDim_p11","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall.not_two_le_seminormalDim_p11","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/SeminormalDimSmall.lean#L103-L107","doc":"`f^{(1,1)} = 1`, so its block is `M₁(ℝ)` and the trace loses nothing there.\n`trace_does_not_separate` needs `2 ≤ f^λ` and genuinely does not apply — recorded\nso the boundary of those results is visible rather than assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall.seminormalDim_p11","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall.seminormalDim_p11","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/SeminormalDimSmall.lean#L100-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall.p11","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.SeminormalDimSmall.p11","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/SeminormalDimSmall.lean#L94-L98","doc":"The partition `(1,1) ⊢ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lea